; Assignment pops a value off the stack like any other consumer. A
; right-hand side that produces none pops whatever is underneath, and pops
; an empty stack when there is nothing there. The empty case exits 1 with no
; message and nothing on stderr.
;
; Run: arturo bugs/stack-underflow-exit.art
; Expected: five lines, ending with "never reached".
; Actual: four lines, then silent exit 1.

x: 1 + 1
print ["control, binds a value that exists:" x]

; a leftover on the stack, and the value-less binding takes it
99
y: print "hi"
print ["bound the leftover instead:" y]

; nothing left on the stack, and the same statement ends the process
z: print "hi again"
print "never reached"
